# Task Brief — Template (v1)

A task brief is the **one** incoming turn that gets a subagent or the next agent
moving. It replaces mid-course correction: where it was complete, the August
corpus ran **6 sessions with 79–266 agent steps and not a single correction**;
the control run with half-finished figures needed **24 correction turns**.

**If one of the five mandatory fields is missing: ask once, don't guess.**
Guessing is exactly the evidenced cost driver — and one transposed digit in a
brief (5 instead of 50 cents) ran unchallenged for 1h 41min and 97 edits across
8 files.

## The five mandatory fields

| Field | What goes in it |
|---|---|
| **Path / location** | Absolute path, file plus section/symbol. No "somewhere in the module". |
| **Symptom** | What is observably wrong — what you see, not what you suspect. |
| **Cause, if known** | The root cause, if known; otherwise explicitly "unknown", never a guess dressed up as a fact. |
| **Measurement / evidence** | The number or artifact the symptom hangs on — with its measurement depth. |
| **Acceptance criterion** | How the brief is recognized as done — checkable against the artifact, not the mechanism (see `rules/slop-prevention.md` Trigger 3). |

## The two additions

- **"Measured, not assumed — PLEASE VERIFY YOURSELF."** States the measurement
  depth and explicitly hands the verification burden back, instead of implying
  certainty. Ten worktree briefs in this format all ran through in **one
  turn each**, and two of them refused — with reasons — a weakening or an
  unrequested refactor; the refusal was accepted.
- **"What is explicitly NOT part of this brief."** The negative list is the
  cheapest scope brake there is: it costs one line and turns scope creep into
  a visible deviation instead of a judgment call. It gets checked not only
  when writing, but again at **every** later expansion — that's part of the
  wave review in `agents/control-agent.md` §4, "Scope against the
  negative-list" (IMP-201).

## Raw form (copy this)

```markdown
## Task: <one sentence, what is to be achieved>

- **Location:** <absolute path + section/symbol>
- **Symptom:** <what is observably wrong>
- **Cause, if known:** <root cause — or explicitly "unknown">
- **Measurement / evidence:** <number/artifact + measurement depth> —
  measured, not assumed; PLEASE VERIFY YOURSELF.
- **Acceptance criterion:** <checkable against the artifact>
- **Not part of this task:** <what explicitly stays out>
- **Verbatim user instruction:** "<quote, if one exists>"
```

The last field is omitted if there is no verbatim instruction. If one exists,
it is **passed on as a quote, never paraphrased** — and the subagent may not
replace it with its own judgment, only escalate it upward
(`agents/control-agent.md` §3).

## Filled-in example

```markdown
## Task: The weekly run actually evaluates the compressed signal shards.

- **Location:** `~/.claude/scheduled-tasks/weekly-improve/SKILL.md`, Step 3
  (signal evaluation)
- **Symptom:** The run reports "ok" and produces findings, but none of them
  come from a `.gz` shard.
- **Cause, if known:** BSD `zcat` reads a `.gz` file as empty and exits 0 —
  no error, no output, no note in the log.
- **Measurement / evidence:** The 2026-07-26 run missed 1,286 signals;
  `gunzip -c` on the same file outputs them. Measured, not assumed —
  PLEASE VERIFY YOURSELF.
- **Acceptance criterion:** The same step, run over the same shard, outputs
  >0 lines; line count before/after in the report.
- **Not part of this task:** no change to the findings logic, no rework of
  the rotation scheme, no new data sources.
```

## Where it's used

| Where | How |
|---|---|
| Subagent dispatch | Mandatory form for every task text — `agents/control-agent.md` §2/§3 |
| Handoff between sessions | Mandatory form for "Next recommended action" — `commands/handoff.md` Step 4 |
| Own diagnoses to the user | FINDING format: the same fields, plus "PLEASE VERIFY YOURSELF" |

